{"name":"Kitten","hex":"#d3c7bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kitten","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young cat, especially before sexual maturity (reached at about seven months).","A young rabbit, rat, hedgehog, squirrel, fox, beaver, badger, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give birth to kittens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kitten"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kitten","blocks":[{"text":"A kitten is a juvenile cat. After being born, kittens display primary altriciality and are fully dependent on their mothers for survival. They normally do not open their eyes for seven to ten days. After about two weeks, kittens develop quickly and begin to explore the world beyond their nest. After a further three to four weeks, they begin to eat solid food and grow baby teeth. Domestic kittens are highly social animals and usually enjoy human companionship."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Juvenile_Ragdoll.jpg/330px-Juvenile_Ragdoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitten","wikidata":"Q147"},{"title":"Kitten (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Kitten is an American alternative rock band formed in Los Angeles, California in 2009. It is fronted by vocalist Chloe Chaidez, who founded the band and has been its sole consistent member since its inception. The band is currently based in Los Angeles. Its current members, in addition to Chaidez, are guitarists Dave Stagno and Parker Silzer IV, and keyboardist Max Tsiring."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitten_(band)","wikidata":"Q15044623"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/1_dia_de_vida.jpg/500px-1_dia_de_vida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/1_dia_de_vida.jpg/1280px-1_dia_de_vida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u